   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "common multiple",
     "common factor",
     "co-prime"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A common multiple is a number that is a multiple of both. Common multiples of 4 and 6 include 12 and 24. A common factor divides both numbers, such as 2 for 4 and 6.\nTwo numbers are co-prime when their only common factor is 1. 4 and 9 are co-prime, though neither is prime.\nCo-prime numbers are used to make codes and safe locks."
    }
